𒑰 DUB.SAR 1.0 Example: Unit Conversions and Dimensional Safety
𒑰 Difficulty: Beginner
𒑰 Concept: Units & Dimensional Metrology
𒑰 Mode: Mixed (Cuneiform syntax with Latin identifiers)
𒑰
𒑰 Purpose:
𒑰   Demonstrates physical unit conversions and compile-time dimensional safety
𒑰   across standard metrological dimensions (time, length, mass).
𒑰
𒑰 Expected Output:
𒑰   7200 seconds converted to hours (expected 2 hour):
𒑰   2 hour
𒑰   36 hours converted to days (expected 1;30 day):
𒑰   1;30 𒌓
𒑰   1;30 day converted to minutes (expected 2160 minute):
𒑰   2160 minute
𒑰   36 hour + 12 hour:
𒑰   48 hour

𒂊𒁹

    # Base quantities
    t-sec : 7200 second
    t-min : 180 minute
    t-hr : 36 hour

    # Explicit conversions
    c-hr :
        t-sec
        hour
        𒀝 convert

    c-day :
        t-hr
        𒌓
        𒀝 convert

    c-min :
        c-day
        minute
        𒀝 convert

    # Compatible addition
    total-time :
        t-hr
        12 hour
        𒍣

𒅗𒁹

    𒁹𒀀 "7200 seconds converted to hours (expected 2 hour):"
    𒁹𒀀 c-hr

    𒁹𒀀 "36 hours converted to days (expected 1;30 day):"
    𒁹𒀀 c-day

    𒁹𒀀 "1;30 day converted to minutes (expected 2160 minute):"
    𒁹𒀀 c-min

    𒁹𒀀 "36 hour + 12 hour:"
    𒁹𒀀 total-time
